      "base_or_modification": "paper-specific",
      "summary": "The forecast target is the discretized momentum, read as a transfer from one player to the other. Forty-three indicators are reduced to two components on the first thirty matches, with the Alcaraz match held out to avoid leakage. The biplot is read as evidence that the classes cannot be separated by a line, so the boosted trees replace a simple classifier. The dependent variable is the change of the lead between two consecutive moments. The importance of a factor is its contribution divided by the largest contribution, times 100. Break points average about 96.7 and the point winner scores 74.9. On the held-out match, 231 of 334 moments are correct, which is 69.16 percent. Precision is 0.755, recall 0.633, and the F1 score 0.689. The area under the curve is 0.75 for both classes and for both averages. The conclusion rounds the accuracy up to 70 percent.",
